# The acid's answer (the fourth acid page, ARP x4): its kind (K1), how often in bars or loops of the line (K2, 0.17.21: Sync folded in), which way (K3), its level (K4,
# 0.17.21: the unit's setting, fxs96). The line asks, then answers.
seed 0
wait 500
# (0.17.85) HYPNO 01 answers now (the maker's: an octave up, every 4th): the test starts from no answer
setpar 151 0
setpar 21 0
tap GLO
tap ARP
tap ARP
tap ARP
tap ARP
expect view 15
expect par76 0
# an octave, up one (kind 1 * 5 + direction 3)
spin K1 1
wait 100
expect par151 8
shot answer_page.png
# up two
spin K3 1
wait 100
expect par151 9
# Mirror (kind 4), the direction kept (4): the contour round the line's middle, two octaves up from there
spin K1 3
wait 100
expect par151 24
shot answer_mirror.png
# Reverse, Rotate, Sparse, Accents follow
spin K1 1
wait 100
expect par151 29
shot answer_reverse.png
spin K1 3
wait 100
expect par151 44
# every 4th bar, then before a drum change; the chance
spin K2 2
wait 100
expect par21 2
spin K2 5
wait 100
expect par21 7
# past Drift: the same counts in loops of the line (par76, the old Sync, 1)
spin K2 1
wait 100
expect par21 0
expect par76 1
spin K2 -1
wait 100
expect par21 7
expect par76 0
spin K2 3
wait 100
expect par21 2
expect par76 1
# the answer's level: +4 dB
expect fxs96 0
spin K4 2
wait 100
expect fxs96 2
# (0.17.22) SEL + ARP: the answer on the next bar, though the count (8 bars) is far off; then the count goes on (the bar after: the call)
spin K2 -4
wait 100
expect par21 6
expect par76 0
wait 2500
press SEL
tap ARP
release SEL
waitfor acidans 1 2600
waitfor acidans 0 2600
wait 2500
expect acidans 0
wait 2000
